WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.799 --> 00:00:05.040
Why does Mark Harmon have a reduced role in
Season 19 of "NCIS"?

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:07.880
And what do his cast mates really think of
him?

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:12.760
"NCIS," the CBS police procedural drama, is
currently in the middle of airing its 19th

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:13.760
season.

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:18.320
Having first aired in 2003, the popular series
is nearing two full decades on the air, which

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:21.619
is an impressive feat for just about any television
show.

00:00:21.619 --> 00:00:26.579
Created by Donald P. Bellisario and Don McGill,
"NCIS" follows the Major Case Response Team

00:00:26.579 --> 00:00:30.869
special agents of the Naval Criminal Investigative
Service in Washington, D.C.

00:00:30.869 --> 00:00:34.800
For much of the show's run, the fictional
team was led by Supervisory Special Agent

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:39.510
Leroy Jethro Gibbs, played by Mark Harmon,
who is widely considered the face of the show.

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:44.239
However, in October 2021, The Hollywood Reporter
wrote that Harmon would no longer be working

00:00:44.239 --> 00:00:50.109
on the show as a series regular, with Season
19, Episode 4 acting as a conclusion to Gibbs'

00:00:50.109 --> 00:00:51.629
story, for now.

00:00:51.629 --> 00:00:54.719
Executive producer and showrunner Steven D.
Binder said in a statement,

00:00:54.719 --> 00:00:59.690
"As an executive producer and dear friend,
Mark continues to be an integral part of the

00:00:59.690 --> 00:01:03.880
fabric of the show [...] So regarding the
future of Gibbs, as long-time fans of the

00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:08.000
show may have noticed over the years [...] never
count Leroy Jethro Gibbs out."

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:13.080
Still, Harmon has exited the series, at least
for the time being, leaving fans to reflect

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:14.080
on his legacy.

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:18.940
Luckily for us, TV Insider gathered up comments
made about Harmon by his "NCIS" co-stars,

00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:23.291
in which they reveal what it was like to work
with him on the set of the show.

00:01:23.291 --> 00:01:24.920
Naturally, they all have good things to say.

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:29.720
To start with, David McCallum, who plays Dr.
Donald "Ducky" Mallard, credited Harmon with

00:01:29.720 --> 00:01:31.950
creating a productive working environment.

00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:33.680
McCallum said in 2007:

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:38.320
"There was always a certain degree of chaos
[at one point during the series' production],

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:39.770
but it's all gone now.

00:01:39.770 --> 00:01:44.490
Mark was instrumental in putting our house
in order — I really thank him for that."

00:01:44.490 --> 00:01:48.770
In 2009, co-star Michael Weatherly, who played
Senior Field Agent Anthony DiNozzo through

00:01:48.770 --> 00:01:52.250
Season 13, complimented Harmon's on-set behavior,
saying:

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:58.190
"[Harmon is] a very rare person in this business
because there's no assistant, no entourage.

00:01:58.190 --> 00:02:03.850
Mark is largely just a very straightforward,
approachable, calm, assertive guy.

00:02:03.850 --> 00:02:05.430
He's not a people pleaser."

00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:11.120
In 2019, Cote de Pablo, who joined in Season
3 as Special Agent Ziva David, said of Harmon:

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:16.020
"We were always trying to infuse [scenes]
with different things, try something new.

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:19.500
Mark has been here for years, and he's still
bringing it."

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:23.140
Even those closest to Harmon recognize his
impressive professionalism.

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:27.280
Harmon's real-life wife Pam Dawber, who played
Marcie Warren in later seasons, raved about

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:29.130
Harmon in 2021, saying:

00:02:29.130 --> 00:02:32.530
"Mark is for the best of everybody and everything.

00:02:32.530 --> 00:02:34.160
His ego does not extend.

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:36.530
He just wants it all to work."

00:02:36.530 --> 00:02:41.550
We'll definitely all miss Harmon's on-screen
presence in "NCIS," just as his co-stars will

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:44.390
miss him both on and off the screen.

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:49.000
Being that Leroy Jethro Gibbs was the head
of NCIS' Major Case Response Team, Mark Harmon

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:50.880
was considered the lead of the show.

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:55.090
As the lead actor on the series, Harmon's
role came with different responsibilities

00:02:55.090 --> 00:02:56.900
than the other roles in the cast.

00:02:56.900 --> 00:03:01.659
Sean Murray, who plays Tim McGee, told Country
Living that Mark Harmon was "number one,"

00:03:01.659 --> 00:03:02.659
and explained,

00:03:02.659 --> 00:03:08.319
"We wouldn't be here, 16 years later, if it
wasn't for Harmon [...] Harmon is a very special

00:03:08.319 --> 00:03:09.490
individual."

00:03:09.490 --> 00:03:13.730
During an interview with Build, Cote de Pablo
also revealed that Harmon was one of her mentors.

00:03:13.730 --> 00:03:16.819
"He's more of a friend mentor, you know?

00:03:16.819 --> 00:03:21.240
He was always like a father figure to me."

00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:23.540
Referencing their characters, she explained,

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:27.290
"Obviously, Ziva and Gibbs have that but Cote
and Mark have that as well."

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:31.380
When it came to being the lead actor, Michael
Weatherly relied on Harmon's advice when he

00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:34.959
got his own series-lead role on the CBS drama
Bull.

00:03:34.959 --> 00:03:36.500
Weatherly told USA Today,

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:41.819
"It's been very illuminating and given me
a great deal of insight and regard for what

00:03:41.819 --> 00:03:46.310
Mark Harmon was doing all those years [on
"NCIS"] [...] When I was like, 'How come he

00:03:46.310 --> 00:03:48.910
doesn't have as much fun as the rest of us?'"

00:03:48.910 --> 00:03:53.430
It's clear that Harmon remains beloved by
viewers and cast members alike.

